# 🟡 Level 2 – Variables, Input & Conditions

## Variables

```bash
#!/bin/bash

name="Akshay"

echo "Welcome $name"
```

---

## User Input

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Enter your name:"
read name

echo "Hello $name"
```

---

## Built-in Variables

| Variable    | Meaning           |
| ----------- | ----------------- |
| `$USER`     | Current user      |
| `$HOME`     | Home directory    |
| `$PWD`      | Current directory |
| `$HOSTNAME` | Computer name     |

Example:

```bash
echo $USER
echo $HOME
```

---

## If Statement

```bash
#!/bin/bash

age=20

if [ $age -ge 18 ]
then
    echo "Adult"
else
    echo "Minor"
fi
```

---

## Case Statement

```bash
read option

case $option in
1)
echo "Start"
;;
2)
echo "Stop"
;;
*)
echo "Invalid"
;;
esac
```

---

# 🟠 Level 3 – Loops & Functions

## For Loop

```bash
for i in 1 2 3 4 5
do
    echo $i
done
```

Output:

```text
1
2
3
4
5
```

---

## While Loop

```bash
count=1

while [ $count -le 5 ]
do
    echo $count
    count=$((count+1))
done
```

---

## Functions

```bash
greet(){

echo "Welcome to Linux"

}

greet
```

